{"content":[{"c":["EBER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Abraham’s ancestor (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.21-25","r":"Gen.10.21-25","rawR":"Gen.10.21-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.21-25","value":"Gen.10.21-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:21-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.14-17","r":"Gen.11.14-17","rawR":"Gen.11.14-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.14-17","value":"Gen.11.14-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:14-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.18-25","r":"1Chr.1.18-25","rawR":"1Chr.1.18-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.18-25","value":"1Chr.1.18-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:18-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.35","r":"Luke.3.35","rawR":"Luke.3.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.35","value":"Luke.3.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:35"},") from whom the word “Hebrew” may be derived. Eber lived 464 years and was the ancestor of the “sons of Eber,” a phrase possibly equal to the “Hebrews,” as “sons of Heth” equals the “Hittites” (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.23.10","r":"Gen.23.10","rawR":"Gen.23.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.23.10","value":"Gen.23.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 23:10"},", ",{"c":["nasb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). However, the term “Hebrew” may be an indication of social class rather than of descent from Eber. Eber had a son in whose time the earth was divided, a division possibly into nomadic and sedentary groups."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Gadite leader registered during the reigns of Jothan, king of Judah (950–932 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), and Jeroboam II, king of Israel (993–953 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.13","r":"1Chr.5.13","rawR":"1Chr.5.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.13","value":"1Chr.5.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:13"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Heber”)."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Benjamite and Elpaal’s descendant (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.12","r":"1Chr.8.12","rawR":"1Chr.8.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.12","value":"1Chr.8.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Benjamite and Shashak’s descendant (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.22","r":"1Chr.8.22","rawR":"1Chr.8.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.22","value":"1Chr.8.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Head of Amok’s priestly family during the days of the high priest Joiakim (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.20","r":"Neh.12.20","rawR":"Neh.12.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.20","value":"Neh.12.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eber","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:21-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.21-25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.21-25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.21-25"},{"anchorText":"11:14-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.14-17","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.14-17","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.14-17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:18-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.18-25","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.18-25","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.18-25"},{"anchorText":"Lk 3:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.35","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.35","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.35"},{"anchorText":"Gn 23:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.23.10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.23.10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.23.10"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.13","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.13","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.12","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.12","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.12"},{"a